      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2013 Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "Herein we report a case of cat scratch disease on account of its atypical presentation."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "PATIENTS AND METHODS",
            "content": "A 21-year-old woman presented erythema nodosum associated with painful bilateral inguinal adenopathy, odynophagia, joint pain and evening urticaria in a setting of impaired general condition. Initial serological testing for Bartonella henselae was negative. PCR for Bartonella henselae performed on an adenectomy fragment was positive. A favourable outcome was achieved with azithromycin."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "COMMENTS",
            "content": "This case shows an atypical and severe presentation of cat scratch disease and raises the problem of sensitivity of serotyping."
          }
        ]
      },
